# Demon Wall: "As long as this creature has a counter on it, it can attack as though it didn't have defender" is a
# permission checked as attackers are declared (CR 508.1a, 508.1c, 609.4), not a reason to leave combat afterwards. Bot1's
# Wall gets two +1/+1 counters on turn 3 and attacks on turn 5 as a 5/5. In the declare attackers step, after the
# declaration, Bot2 sacrifices Vampire Hexmage to remove all its counters: the Wall is a 3/3 with defender again, still an
# attacking creature (CR 506.4: nothing removed it from combat), and deals Bot2 3 combat damage.

